## 4. LLM API design (`llm_client.py`)

Transport: OpenAI-compatible `POST {base_url}/v1/chat/completions` via `urllib.request`,
key from env `AUTOTENDER_LLM_API_KEY`. **Structured output per server** (verified on
primary docs; keep the tolerant parser anyway — value-level errors like `"5 Stk"` in
`quantity` survive any syntactic guarantee):

  | Server | Request | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | llama.cpp `llama-server` | `response_format: {"type":"json_schema","schema":…}` (also non-std `json_schema` field) | json_schema→GBNF; `cache_prompt` default true — bit-exactness not guaranteed across batch sizes, don't expect byte-identical reruns |
  | vLLM ≥0.12 | `structured_outputs: {"json":…}` / `StructuredOutputsParams(json=…)` | **`guided_json` REMOVED in v0.12.0** (sibling's round-1 name outdated); backends xgrammar/guidance (outlines, lm-format-enforcer for regex) |
  | Ollama | native `/api/chat` `format: <schema>` | most reliable via native API, not the OpenAI shim; docs still say "also instruct the model to respond in JSON" |
  | OpenAI/Z.ai | `response_format: {"type":"json_schema","strict": true}` | strict: all keys `required`, `additionalProperties:false`, no `allOf/not/if-then-else` (else HTTP error) |

  Client tactic: send `response_format` json_schema AND inline the schema in the prompt
  (cheap servers ignore unknown fields; strict ones enforce).
- **Backoff** (per OpenAI rate-limit guide): honor `Retry-After` as a **minimum** + jitter
  (parallel workers must not sync); else exponential backoff with jitter (1 s base, ×2, cap
  30 s); cap BOTH attempts (3) and total time; retry only 429/5xx/timeout, never 4xx
  auth/quota; retries only in `llm_client.py` so layers can't multiply requests.
- **LoRA** (llama.cpp README): read `../web_ui/ui_settings.json` read-only →
  `tasks.input_processing.selected` + `base_model`; resolve vs `advanced.loras_dir=/data/loras`.
  One server: `--model <base> --lora <a1> --lora-init-without-apply`; switch per request via
  `lora: [{"id": n, "scale": 1.0}]` or `POST /lora-adapters` — **no restart on UI change**;
  different LoRA configs are not batched together; comparator = plain base (`lora: []`).
  HF LoRAs need `convert_lora_to_gguf.py`; vLLM `--enable-lora` takes HF adapters directly.
  Env override `AUTOTENDER_INPUT_LORA`. `selected: null` ⇒ run base model (R3.9).
- `settings.yaml`: final authoritative sketch in R3.2 (round-2 sketch superseded).
- All prompts: system pins "German Swiss HVAC Leistungsverzeichnis", temperature 0, JSON-only,
  every answer cites `source_page` + verbatim snippet; the comparator re-checks exactly those
  citations (claims evidenced by verbatim source text).

