### R3.6 Comparator & matcher (pseudocode)

```
verify_rules(pos, page):                     # free tier
    ok_p   = pos.source_page in section_pages
    ok_q   = all(tok in page for tok in tokens(pos.quantity_raw))          # "Stk","5"
    ok_d   = all(dim_literal in page for dim in parse_dims(pos))           # "10 x", "DN100"
    ok_s   = partial_ratio(pos.raw_source_snippet, page) >= 90   # rapidfuzz (installed);
          # verbatim German snippet scores 100 on real rows vs <=43 for translated/fake
          # text (agent 2 R3.4 + R4 cross-check); difflib ratio >= 0.75 as no-dep fallback
    return confirmed  if all four
           borderline if ok_p and one of ok_q/ok_d fails   # -> tier 2 llm
           rejected   otherwise
extract pipeline: extract -> verify_rules each row -> borderline/failed -> verify_llm ->
  corrected take fixes -> rejected to pos_NN.rejected.csv -> ONE repair_round ("finde die
  echte Position nahe Seite X") -> still-rejected stay side-file.
match_position(pos, catalog):
    d = parse_dims(pos.description + technical_attributes + snippet)
    cands = [pr for pr in catalog if pr.unit == pos.unit
             and not (d.dn and pr.dn and d.dn != pr.dn)
             and not (d.wh and pr.wh and d.wh != pr.wh)
             and category_compatible(pos.category, pr.category)]
    for pr in cands: s = token_set_ratio(pos.desc_normalized_english, pr.desc)   # DESC ONLY
                      # attr/mfr are NOT score weights (mfr ~always 0 vs Demo* catalog,
                      # R4.4); they ride along as features for the LLM tie-break prompt
    top = max(cands, s)                     # rapidfuzz (installed, verified R4) else difflib
    if s >= 80: accept; elif s >= 60: llm_tiebreak(top-3) or review; else: unmatched
    if accepted pr.source_type == supplier_package: status=supplier_quote_required
    review_required = (60 <= s < 80) or verdict == corrected or s is None
```

